      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for saying that but resting doesnt really change anything. i wake up and it's just the same pile of bills, the same feeling of being behind, the same pressure to perform when i have nothing left to give. it feels like i'm just stuck in a room with no doors. the more i try to \"fix\" it, the more it falls apart. it's like i'm just waiting for a crash that's already happening. how am i supposed to keep doing this for another thirty years? it feels completely irrational to keep going when everything is just... gone.",
